$OpenBSD$

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Do not run the game server as root. It writes logs, incoming maps, demos,
server state and configuration relative to its working directory.
Prepare a private directory as the user who will run the server:

    mkdir -m 700 ~/.assaultcube-server
    cp -R ${TRUEPREFIX}/share/assaultcube/config ~/.assaultcube-server/
    cp -R ${TRUEPREFIX}/share/assaultcube/packages ~/.assaultcube-server/
    mkdir -p ~/.assaultcube-server/logs ~/.assaultcube-server/demos

Review config/servercmdline.txt and the upstream server documentation.
Then run assaultcube-server with the required server options. The launcher
uses ~/.assaultcube-server, or AC_SERVER_HOME if explicitly set, and never
writes the package's shared data. Keep this private copy updated when the
package's configuration/maps change. No public server is started at install.

Upstream's public-server/master-registration behavior and legacy protocol
need native interoperability and security testing before public deployment.
